   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the county of Suffolk to convey by\nappropriate instruments to the Hampton Bays Water District, an easement in\nMeschutt Beach County Park, for installation of a subaqueous water pipe\ncrossing",
    "basePrintNo": "S9317",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9317-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9317\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the county of Suffolk to convey by\nappropriate instruments to the Hampton Bays Water District, an easement\nin Meschutt Beach County Park, for installation of a subaqueous water\npipe crossing\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to provide the Town of Southampton authori-\nzation to alienate the Meschutt Beach County Park for the purposes of a\ncapital project.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the County of Suffolk to convey an easement in\nMeschutt Beach County Park for the installation of a subaqueous water\npipe crossing.\n\nSection 2. Establishes that the authorization shall only be effective\nupon the condition that the county of Suffolk dedicate an amount equal\nto or greater than the fair market value of the easement interest being\nalienated to the acquisition of new parklands and/or capital improve-\nments to existing park and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 3. Metes and bounds of parcel for authorized easement.\n\nSection 4. Provides that the easement shall not occur until the county\nof Suffolk has complied with any federal requirements pertaining to the\nalienation or conversion of parklands.\n\nSection 5. Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of Southampton requires an act of the State Legislature to\nalienate a parcel of parkland known as the Meschutt Beach County Park to\ninitiate the installation of a subaqueous water pipe crossing a water\nmain extension under the Shinnecock Canal. This capital project will\nimprove water supply, water pressure, and fire protection in the parcel\nand surrounding lands.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNo fiscal implications for the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
